LLM TASK RECIPES (READ-ONLY FIRST)

A. Discover capability
  get_manual() -> get_manual(topic='devices') -> help pwmctl
  ps
  ip
  pins
Read only the relevant page. A missing Linux option is not a bug.

B. Compile a C program
  get_manual(topic='languages/c')
  get_manual(topic='c-examples')
  write_file(path='/tmp/demo.c', content='...')
  cc /tmp/demo.c
  cat /tmp/demo.s
  as /tmp/demo.s
  /tmp/a.out
Check compiler and assembler success independently; as always
replaces /tmp/a.out. cc accepts no #include. Keep source <=1024 B.

C. Assemble hand-written Thumb-1
  get_manual(topic='languages/asm')
  write_file(path='/tmp/demo.s', content='...')
  as /tmp/demo.s
  /tmp/a.out
Use only implemented instructions; emitted PNX1 binary is PIC.

D. Run a Python-like script without a REPL
  get_manual(topic='languages/python')
  write_file(path='/tmp/demo.py', content='print(1 + 2)\n')
  python /tmp/demo.py
Do not launch bare 'python' via MCP: that enters a REPL.

E. Inspect memory
  ps
  mem -s
  mem -s sh
  hexdump /dev/shm 0 64
  hexdump /dev/mem 0x20000000 32
Read /man/memory before using hardware addresses. /dev/mem
requires offset + count; addresses have architecture meanings.

F. Investigate system calls
  trace on -s
  ps
  trace show
  trace on
Use trace on -a only when full internal events are needed.
trace show disables recording; restore with trace on afterwards.

G. Device control after user authorization
  pins
  pwmctl status
  pwmctl freq 523
  pwmctl status
  pwmctl off
Never change assigned communication pins or drive outputs before
checking owners and connected hardware. See /man/devices.
